{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.bar_symmetric_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.bar_symmetric_iff","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L98-L112","doc":"**The bar involution is a symmetry of the colour fibre exactly at\n`z = 0`.**  Together with `z = s - s⁻¹`, that is `s = s⁻¹`, i.e. `q = 1`:\nthe matter and antimatter colour curves coincide only at the interface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.degenerate_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.degenerate_iff","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L83-L96","doc":"**The degeneration locus is the single point `z = -1`.**  The golden\nratio enters only when this one condition is pulled back along `z = s - s⁻¹`\nand `q = s²`, where it acquires the two preimages `q = φ⁻²` and `q = φ²`.\n`rem:golden-ratio-degeneration` records only the first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.bar_cofactor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.bar_cofactor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L80-L81","doc":"`4z² + 3 > 0` for every real `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.quadratic_factor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.quadratic_factor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L76-L78","doc":"`4z² - z + 4 > 0` for every real `z` (discriminant `1 - 64 = -63 < 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.bar_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.bar_defect","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L64-L70","doc":"**The bar defect.**  `q ↦ q⁻¹` sends `z ↦ -z`, and the Weierstrass\ncoefficient fails to be even by exactly `10 z (4z² + 3)`.  This is the\nframework's matter/antimatter asymmetry of the colour fibration, and it is\nderived rather than posited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.z_odd_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.z_odd_inv","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L59-L62","doc":"`z = s - s⁻¹` is **odd** under `s ↦ s⁻¹`, the sign-preserving lift of\n`q ↦ q⁻¹`.  Since `weierstrassR27` is not even (`bar_defect` below), that\nlift is *not* a symmetry of the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.z_invariant_neg_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.z_invariant_neg_inv","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`z = s - s⁻¹` is **invariant** under `s ↦ -s⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.s_form_eq_z_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.s_form_eq_z_form","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L44-L54","doc":"**The two presentations agree.**  The `s`-polynomial of\n`rem:golden-ratio-degeneration` equals `s³` times the `z`-polynomial of\n`t-duality-elliptic.md`, once `z` is replaced by `s - s⁻¹`.  Needs a field\n(the substitution inverts `s`), so this is the one statement here that is\nnot over a bare `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.weierstrassR27_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.weierstrassR27_factor","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L38-L42","doc":"`weierstrassR27` factors as `5(z+1)(4z² - z + 4)`.  The linear factor\nis the whole real degeneration locus; see `degenerate_iff` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.weierstrassR27","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BringsSurface.ColourCurveModulus.weierstrassR27","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringsSurface/ColourCurveModulus.lean#L32-L36","doc":"The second Weierstrass coefficient of the colour elliptic fibre, as a\npolynomial in the spacetime ratio `z`.  This is the form given in\n`t-duality-elliptic.md`: `q_W(z) = 5(4z³ + 3z² + 3z + 4)/27`, here cleared\nof its denominator so the statement lives over any `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}